.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBContainer\fR: centers its content and limits its width to a named size, after Mantine's Container. The base of a content page: every page reads at the same width whatever the window, and the same sizes name the same widths everywhere.
.PP
| Size | Max width | | \-\-\- | \-\-\- | | \fBContainerSize::Xs\fR | 540 | | \fBContainerSize::Sm\fR | 720 | | \fBContainerSize::Md\fR (default) | 960 | | \fBContainerSize::Lg\fR | 1140 | | \fBContainerSize::Xl\fR | 1320 |
.IP \(bu 2
The width includes the padding (border\-box), so a \fBMd\fR container with the default padding holds content 960 minus both sides.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfluid\fR drops the limit: the container fills its parent.
.IP \(bu 2
The padding is horizontal by default, \fBMetrics::page_padding\fR each side (Mantine's container pads the sides only). \fBpadding\fR takes any \fBPadding\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
A container does not scroll. Put it in a \fBscrolled_window\fR for a page (\fBPage\fR does).
.PP
.nf
.RS
scrolled_window(Container::new(content).size(ContainerSize::Sm))
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBAdwClamp\fR is the same idea in pixels; this is the named\-size form.
